<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Dickinsonia costata cellular Turing wavelength, 56 µm, White Sea 558 Ma (Pass 1) (Dickinsonia costata)",
        "Dickinsonia costata cellular Turing wavelength, 56 µm, White Sea 558 Ma (Pass 1) faithfully reproduces Dickinsonia costata morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Dickinsonia costata specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Dickinsonia costata" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That the Pass 1 spot lattice is a fitted rendering of this specimen.",
        "does_not_claim: That the centimetre-scale modules in the photograph are 56 µm apart.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Nondimensional Du, Dv, a, b for a 56 µm pitch, distinct from the 2.2 mm sibling.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Spectral integration and a single-run wavenumber measurement.",
        "reported_in_source: Bobrovskiy et al. 2018: White Sea Dickinsonia preserves cholesteroids; age 558 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Evans et al. 2017 and 2021: ovoid outline and posterior module addition.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: 56 µm is this slot's cellular-tier assignment, not a length Bobrovskiy or Evans measured on the fossil.",
        "transfer_boundary: Evans' morphometrics are mostly South Australian; the age pin is the White Sea horizon." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Dickinsonia costata (Late Ediacaran (White Sea, 558 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Zoophyta & Vermes (Cnidaria/Platyhelminthes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Dickinsonia" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/dickinsonia_costata_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Dickinsonia costata; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics. | Bobrovskiy et al. 2018: White Sea Dickinsonia preserves cholesteroids; age 558 Ma. | Evans et al. 2017 and 2021: ovoid outline and posterior module addition.; reconstructed_in_script: Nondimensional Du, Dv, a, b for a 56 µm pitch, distinct from the 2.2 mm sibling. | Spectral integration and a single-run wavenumber measurement.; transfer_boundary: 56 µm is this slot's cellular-tier assignment, not a length Bobrovskiy or Evans measured on the fossil. | Evans' morphometrics are mostly South Australian; the age pin is the White Sea horizon.; does_not_claim: That the centimetre-scale modules in the photograph are 56 µm apart. | That the Pass 1 spot lattice is a fitted rendering of this specimen.]; phenomenon_size: 44 µm (4.42e-05 m, log10=-4.355 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 44 µm to 9.9 cm): 44 µm:dickinsonia-costata-bioelectric-polarity, 138 µm:dickinsonia-costata-vertex-packing, 2.2 mm:dickinsonia-costata-turing-wavelength, 4.4 mm:dickinsonia-costata-clock-wavefront, 9.9 mm:dickinsonia-costata-morphogen-condensation, 1.2 cm:dickinsonia-costata-elastic-buckling, 1.4 cm:dickinsonia-costata-flux-canalization, 1.9 cm:dickinsonia-costata-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/pab.2021.31>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2017.1348>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aat7228>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0176874> ;
    pk:externalAtlasDataset <https://paleobiodb.org/classic/checkTaxonInfo?taxon_name=Dickinsonia>,
        <https://www.morphosource.org/Search/index?search=Dickinsonia> ;
